# {{ project_name }}

{{ description }}

Generated from [ai-engineering-framework](https://github.com/flam7791/ai-engineering-framework)
(pattern P1: governed retrieval with a sensitivity ceiling). Owner: **{{ owner }}**.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    Q[Question] --> G1{Question checks}
    G1 --> R[Keyword retrieval<br/>documents at or below<br/>'{{ classification_ceiling }}' only]
    R -- nothing relevant --> NF[Not found<br/>no model call]
    R --> M[Model<br/>local by default]
    M --> V{Validator<br/>cites a given source?<br/>links allowed?}
    V -- yes --> A[Answer + citations]
    V -- no --> W[Withheld, with reason]
    A & W & NF --> L[(Audit line<br/>no question text)]
```

- **Local first.** The default model is `{{ local_model }}` through [Ollama](https://ollama.com),
  so nothing leaves the machine. Any OpenAI-compatible endpoint (vLLM on a GPU server, an LLM
  gateway, a cloud deployment in your tenant) is a change of two settings, not of code.
- **Guardrails in code.** Documents above the ceiling are never loaded. An answer is released
  only if it cites a source it was given and links only to allowed domains.
- **Evaluated.** `evals/cases.jsonl` covers answers, citations, a planted prompt injection, a
  withheld document and out-of-scope questions. CI runs it on every push.

## Quick start

```bash
python -m venv .venv
# Windows: .venv\Scripts\activate      macOS/Linux: source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -e ".[dev]"
pytest                                   # offline, no model needed
{{ project_slug }} eval --model standin  # the evaluation with the deterministic stand-in
```

### With a local open-weight model (Ollama)

```bash
ollama pull {{ local_model }}
{{ project_slug }} ask "How many days do I have to submit an expense claim?"
{{ project_slug }} serve                 # http://127.0.0.1:8000/health, POST /answer
```

### Record a live evaluation, replay it in CI

```bash
{{ project_slug }} eval --model live --recordings evals/recordings/local \
    --out evals/results/local.json --min-pass 0
{{ project_slug }} eval --model replay --recordings evals/recordings/local   # offline, free
```

Commit `evals/recordings/local` and `evals/results/local.json`. CI then replays the run on
every push: a change to the prompt, the retrieval or the documents shows up as a replay miss.
Record a second folder against another endpoint (a larger local model, a gateway, a cloud model)
to compare quality, latency and tokens on the same cases.

### Containers

```bash
docker compose --profile standin up -d --build --wait   # no model: stand-in, for a demo
docker compose --profile local up -d --build --wait     # app + Ollama
docker compose exec ollama ollama pull {{ local_model }}
```

## Configuration

Environment variables, prefixed `{{ package_name | upper }}_`:

| Variable | Default | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `MODEL_BASE_URL` | `http://localhost:11434/v1` | Any OpenAI-compatible endpoint |
| `MODEL_NAME` | `{{ local_model }}` | Model or deployment name |
| `MODEL_API_KEY` | none | Not needed for a local model; use a secret store otherwise |
| `CORPUS_DIR` | `corpus` | Markdown documents with front matter |
| `MAX_CLASSIFICATION` | `{{ classification_ceiling }}` | Documents above it are never loaded |
| `ALLOWED_LINK_DOMAINS` | `aurora.example` | Comma-separated |
| `TOP_K` / `MIN_SCORE` | `4` / `0.5` | Retrieval |

